silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_01_sections_01_concrete_anchor_inclusion#identitycarryoveronpreexistinglegs a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.15.chapters.01.sections.01.concrete_anchor.inclusion#identitycarryoveronpreexistinglegs" .
silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_01_sections_01_concrete_anchor_inclusion#identitycarryoveronpreexistinglegs silm:hasLongDescription "The IdentityCarryoverOnPreExistingLegs is At each pre-existing leg of stage n (HeadObs77, BodyMassQuality77, etc.), the component of i_{n,n+1} is the identity arrow in C. On the new legs admitted at stage n+1 (e.g. MicrochipIdentifier9), the natural transformation has no component because those legs are not in J_Mittens^n. The inclusion never modifies a pre-existing arrow." .
